sey_queenofclean", "song_name": "Original audio", "uses_original_audio": true, "should_mute_audio": false, "should_mute_audio_reason": "", "audio_id": "27732550903076802"}, "ownerUsername": "lynsey_queenofclean", "ownerFullName": "Lynsey Queen Of Clean", "history": [{"date": "2026-08-09", "plays": 29973, "likes": -1, "comments": 31}, {"date": "2026-08-16", "plays": 42647, "likes": -1, "comments": 33}, {"date": "2026-08-23", "plays": 46356, "likes": -1, "comments": 34}, {"date": "2026-08-30", "plays": 46848, "likes": -1, "comments": 34}], "still_climbing": false, "transcript": "I really enjoy answering some of your questions in the shops, we're going to actually show you the products to use. So we've got a couple of questions today, we're going to kick off with question one. So we're going to answer today's question in Poundland. This time of year in particular, I'm always asked about how to keep white socks white, and I think people want them looking pristine. There's nothing worse than having someone come round your house, they've got white socks on and the sole is black. So when it comes to cleaning white socks, when you choose your laundry products, you want to go for bio, not non-bio. Bio is so much better at busting those stains. And I would have one of these in your cupboard. So this is the elbow grease, it's like a bar of soap, but it's a stain remover bar of soap. So I would literally put your hand in the sock, really scrub it with the bar of soap, or use like a washboard, old school washboard, and that's going to really help loosen those stains. And I would add a big generous scoop of bicarbonate of soda to the wash. I'm Poundland and they call it baking soda in here, it's literally the same thing. So that is how you keep your white socks pristine.", "is_relevant": true, "hook_type": "Education"}, {"shortCode": "DbtAYQ7M4LM", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbtAYQ7M4LM/", "caption": "AD - First impressions\u2026 I\u2019m impressed!\n\nI\u2019ve finally 